title: Second <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> Congress
subtitle: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> decides their fate...
view-if: year == 1930 and month == 11 and lvp_timer_1_trigger and lvp_formed
on-arrival: {!
Q.heuss_points = 0;
Q.dietrich_points = 0;
Q.luther_points = 4;
Q.curtius_points = 1;
Q.dingeldey_points = 0;
Q.opposition_points = 0;

if (Q.in_grand_coalition || Q.in_weimar_coalition) {
    Q.lvp_relation += 5;
    Q.lvp_left += 2;
} else if (Q.in_popular_front || Q.in_left_front) {
    Q.lvp_right += 4;
    Q.lvp_relation -= 8;
}

if (Q.agriculture_minister_party == "LVP" || Q.economic_minister_party == "LVP" || (Q.chancellor == "Askew" && !Q.marcher_in_government)) {
    Q.dietrich_points += 2;
}

if (Q.foreign_minister_party == "LVP" || (Q.chancellor == "Askew" && !Q.marcher_in_government)) {
    Q.curtius_points += 2;
}

if (Q.marcher_votes >= 30) {
    Q.dingeldey_points += 2;
}

if (Q.chancellor == "Askew" && Q.marcher_toleration) {
    Q.dietrich_points += 1;
    Q.curtius_points -= 1;
    Q.luther_points -= 1;
    Q.dingeldey_points += 1;
    Q.lvp_right += 3;
}

if (Q.lvp_relation >= 50) {
    Q.lvp_left += 3;
    Q.heuss_points += 1;
    Q.dingeldey_points -= 1;
} else if (Q.lvp_relation < 50) {
    Q.lvp_right += 3;
    Q.dingeldey_points += 1;
    Q.heuss_points -= 1;
}

if (Q.nationalism >= 50) {
    Q.dingeldey_points += 1;
    Q.lvp_right += 1;
}

if (Q.pro_republic >= 70) {
    Q.heuss_points += 2;
    Q.lvp_left += 2;
} else if (Q.pro_republic < 70) {
    Q.dingeldey_points += 1;
    Q.lvp_right += 2;
}

if (Q.lvp_votes >= 11.5) {
    if (Q.lvp_ideology == "Right") {
        Q.lvp_left += 3;
    } else if (Q.lvp_ideology == "Left") {
        Q.lvp_right += 3;
    }
    Q.luther_points += 5;
}

if (Q.heartland_leader == "Lytton") {
    Q.luther_points += 3;
}

if (Q.lvp_right > (Q.lvp_left*1.5) || (Q.lvp_right > (Q.lvp_left + 5))) {
    Q.lvp_ideology = "Right"
} else if (Q.lvp_left > (Q.lvp_right*1.5) || (Q.lvp_left > (Q.lvp_right + 5))) {
    Q.lvp_ideology = "Left"
} else {
    Q.lvp_ideology = "Moderate"
}

if (Q.lvp_ideology == "Right") {
   Q.dingeldey_points += 2;
   Q.curtius_points += 1;
}
if (Q.lvp_ideology == "Moderate") {
    Q.luther_points += 3;
    Q.dietrich_points += 1;
    Q.curtius_points += 1;
}
if (Q.lvp_ideology == "Left") {
    Q.heuss_points += 3;
    Q.dietrich_points += 1;
}

if (Q.curtius_resign_lvp || (Q.curtius_banking_crisis && Q.banking_crisis_seen)) {
    Q.dietrich_points += Math.round(Q.curtius_points * 2 / 3);
    Q.dingeldey_points += Math.round(Q.curtius_points / 3);
    Q.curtius_points = 0;
}

Q.opposition_points = Q.heuss_points + Q.dietrich_points + Q.curtius_points + Q.dingeldey_points

if (Q.heuss_points >= Q.dietrich_points && Q.heuss_points >= Q.curtius_points && Q.heuss_points >= Q.dingeldey_points) {
    Q.heuss_lead = 1;
} else {
    Q.heuss_lead = 0;
}

if (Q.dietrich_points >= Q.heuss_points && Q.dietrich_points >= Q.curtius_points && Q.dietrich_points >= Q.dingeldey_points) {
    Q.dietrich_lead = 1;
} else {
    Q.dietrich_lead = 0;
}

if (Q.curtius_points >= Q.heuss_points && Q.curtius_points >= Q.dietrich_points && Q.curtius_points >= Q.dingeldey_points) {
    Q.curtius_lead = 1;
} else {
    Q.curtius_lead = 0;
}

if (Q.dingeldey_points >= Q.heuss_points && Q.dingeldey_points >= Q.dietrich_points && Q.dingeldey_points >= Q.curtius_points) {
    Q.dingeldey_lead = 1;
} else {
    Q.dingeldey_lead = 0;
}

if (!Q.dietrich_lead && !Q.heuss_lead && !Q.dingeldey_lead && !Q.curtius_lead) {
    Q.lvp_deadlock = 1;
} else {
    Q.lvp_deadlock = 0;
}

!}
max-visits: 1
tags: event
face-image: img/weimar_coalition_3.jpg
new-page: true

= Second <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> Party Congress

The merger of two notoriously factionalized parties has unsurprisingly introduced great dysfunction into the internal politics of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>. Not even a unifying figure like Hans Lytton has been able to quell the endless bickering among the party's factions. The economic calamity has only deepened these divisions, with disagreements arising even on broadly supported issues like parliamentary government, making unified action nearly impossible.

[? if chancellor == "Askew" and not marcher_in_government: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> has shifted significantly to the right due to their participation in [? if in_right_coalition: Askew's center-right coalition?][? if not in_right_coalition: Askew's emergency government?]. This election will be pivotal in determining their policy of cooperation with us in the foreseeable future.?] While Hans Lytton is expected to secure re-election, scattered candidates from across the party could emerge if the majority loses confidence in Lytton's leadership.

- @luther: The party votes...
- @luther_fail: The party votes...

@luther
view-if: luther_points >= opposition_points
on-arrival: lvp_relation += 3; lvp_left += 2
face-image: img/portraits/luther.jpg

Hans Lytton is expectedly re-elected as the leader of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>. He will navigate the party through the economic calamity and will hopefully try to maintain propertied backing for the Unity system.

@luther_fail
view-if: opposition_points > luther_points
on-arrival: {!
Q.luther_endorsed_candidate = "None"

if (Q.lvp_ideology == "Right") {
    Q.luther_endorsed_candidate = "Soren Coalfax"
} else if (Q.lvp_ideology == "Moderate") {
    Q.luther_endorsed_candidate = "Julius Curthose"
} else if (Q.lvp_ideology == "Left") {
    Q.luther_endorsed_candidate = "Albrecht Dietrich"
}

if (Q.lvp_relation >= 65) {
    Q.luther_endorsed_candidate = "Theodor Hewes"
}

if (((Q.curtius_resign_lvp) || (Q.curtius_banking_crisis && Q.banking_crisis_seen)) && Q.luther_endorsed_candidate == "Julius Curthose") {
    Q.luther_endorsed_candidate = "Albrecht Dietrich";
}

if (Q.luther_endorsed_candidate == "Soren Coalfax") {
    Q.dingeldey_points += 1;
} else if (Q.luther_endorsed_candidate == "Julius Curthose") {
    Q.curtius_points += 1;
} else if (Q.luther_endorsed_candidate == "Albrecht Dietrich") {
    Q.dietrich_points += 1;
} else if (Q.luther_endorsed_candidate == "Theodor Hewes") {
    Q.heuss_points += 1;
}

if (Q.heuss_points > Q.dietrich_points && Q.heuss_points > Q.curtius_points && Q.heuss_points > Q.dingeldey_points) {
    Q.heuss_lead = 1;
} else {
    Q.heuss_lead = 0;
}

if (Q.dietrich_points > Q.heuss_points && Q.dietrich_points > Q.curtius_points && Q.dietrich_points > Q.dingeldey_points) {
    Q.dietrich_lead = 1;
} else {
    Q.dietrich_lead = 0;
}

if (Q.curtius_points > Q.heuss_points && Q.curtius_points > Q.dietrich_points && Q.curtius_points > Q.dingeldey_points) {
    Q.curtius_lead = 1;
} else {
    Q.curtius_lead = 0;
}

if (Q.dingeldey_points > Q.heuss_points && Q.dingeldey_points > Q.dietrich_points && Q.dingeldey_points > Q.curtius_points) {
    Q.dingeldey_lead = 1;
} else {
    Q.dingeldey_lead = 0;
}

if (!Q.dietrich_lead && !Q.heuss_lead && !Q.dingeldey_lead && !Q.curtius_lead) {
    Q.lvp_deadlock = 1;
} else {
    Q.lvp_deadlock = 0;
}

!}

Surprisingly, Lytton has failed to command the majority of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> behind his candidacy. Following this result, Lytton has resigned from his chairmanship and now endorses [+ luther_endorsed_candidate +] for the leadership race. Lytton has now taken up a position as the President of the Commonwealth Bank, still holding significant sway over party affairs.

- @heuss
- @dietrich
- @curtius
- @dingeldey
- @deadlock

@heuss
title: Theodor Hewes is elected!
subtitle: Hewes is a <span style="color: #c00000;">Social</span> <span style="color: #000000;">Rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span>, and a member of the former <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>.
unavailable-subtitle: The wider <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span> perceive him as too left-wing, despite his previous affiliation with the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">[+ ddp_name +]</span>'s business wing.
choose-if: heuss_lead
on-arrival: lvp_relation += 12; lvp_left += 7; lvp_leader = "Hewes"; pro_republic += (lvp_votes / 2); commons_lvp += 2; commons_marcher -= 2; burgher_lvp += 4; guild_lvp -= 2; guild_other += 4 if (traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"); guild_traditionalist += 4 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; guild_kvp += 4; landed_lvp -= 4; landed_other += 4 if (traditionalist_ideology == "Radical" and not kvp_formed); landed_traditionalist += 4 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; landed_kvp += 4; faithful_lvp += 2; faithful_marcher -= 2; coalition_dissent -= 1; heuss_explode_time = time + 8; heuss_election_time = time
face-image: img/portraits/heuss.jpg

Theodor Hewes, a rising star and former member of the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>, has been elected chairman of the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">Golds</span>. Backed primarily by the 'Social Republican Circle,' composed of former <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> members and liberal intellectuals and newspapers, Hewes has also garnered support from the broader party due to his decently conservative stances on economic and national issues.

Hewes's victory empowers the '<span style="color: #c00000;">Social</span> <span style="color: #000000;">Rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span>' wing, strengthening our cooperation. Despite his personal leanings toward the right, Hewes remains one of the most committed and genuine supporters for <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberal</span> <span style="color: #586593;">democracy</span> within the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>.

@dietrich
title: Albrecht Dietrich is elected!
subtitle: Dietrich was the former leader of the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>'s business wing, and is somewhat skeptical of cooperation with us.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if not heuss_lead: The wider <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span> perceive him as too left-wing, despite his previous affiliation with the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">[+ ddp_name +]</span>'s business wing. ?][? if heuss_lead: His lack of energy and the burden of his governmental roles have led the party to favor Hewes instead. ?]
choose-if: dietrich_lead
on-arrival: lvp_relation += 5; lvp_left += 3; lvp_leader = "Dietrich"; pro_republic += 3; guild_lvp += 3; landed_lvp += 3; burgher_lvp -= 3; dietrich_lvp_explode_time = time + 8; dietrich_election_time = time
face-image: img/portraits/dietrich.jpg

Albrecht Dietrich, formerly affiliated with the business wing of the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>, has been elected chairman of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>. Dietrich is mainly supported by smaller businesses and ruralites, and [? if chancellor == "Askew" and not marcher_in_government: is known for formulating Askew's emergency decrees during his tenure as Finance Minister.?][? if not (chancellor == "Askew" and not marcher_in_government): is known for his fiscal conservatism.?]

Despite this, Dietrich is not as extreme as the guild-masters on the right of the party and remains open to cooperation with us if there is no other majority. However, his leadership has been quite uninspiring, to say the least. [? if agriculture_minister_party == "LVP" or economic_minister_party == "LVP": The responsibilities of his ministry prevent him from being involved in the day-to-day running of his party, which is now delegated to a group of his associates in the business wing. ?]

@curtius
title: Julius Curthose is elected!
subtitle: Curthose was a member of the former <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>, and is a committed Strattonite and member of their left wing. He has since succeeded Stratton on foreign policy matters.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if dingeldey_lead: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span> perceive him as too left-wing, and point out his lackluster record as a successor to Stratton. ?][? if dietrich_lead or heuss_lead: The left wing of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span> wants to elect a former <span style="color: #D3C24D;">[+ ddp_name +]</span> member, to replace Lytton. ?][? if lvp_deadlock: The left wing of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span> wants to elect a former <span style="color: #D3C24D;">[+ ddp_name +]</span> member, while the right wing of the party prefers a more right-wing former <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span> member. ?]
choose-if: curtius_lead
view-if: not curtius_resign_lvp and not (curtius_banking_crisis and banking_crisis_seen)
on-arrival: lvp_relation += 7; lvp_left += 4; lvp_leader = "Curthose"; pro_republic += 3; guild_lvp += 4; burgher_lvp += 4
face-image: img/portraits/curtius.jpg

Julius Curthose, Stratton's successor in foreign affairs and a former member of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>, has won the vote to succeed Lytton for the chairmanship. Curthose is supported by the 'Pragmatic Center', and was put forth as a compromise candidate. 

As a former member of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>'s left wing, he is in favor of closer cooperation with us. However, his leadership has been quite uninspiring, to say the least. [? if foreign_minister_party == "LVP": The responsibilities of the foreign ministry prevent him from being involved in the day-to-day running of his party, which is now delegated to a group of his associates in the 'Pragmatic Center'. ?]

@dingeldey
title: Soren Coalfax is elected.
subtitle: Coalfax was a member of the former <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>, and commonly associated with the industrial-right of the party.
unavailable-subtitle: The right-industrial faction of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">Golds</span> lack the power necessary to install their candidate.
choose-if: dingeldey_lead
on-arrival: lvp_relation -= 6; lvp_right += 3; lvp_leader = "Coalfax"; burgher_lvp -= 5; commons_lvp -= 2; guild_lvp += 4; coalition_dissent += 1; dingeldey_explode_time = time + 8; dingeldey_election_time = time
face-image: img/portraits/dingeldey.jpg

Soren Coalfax, previously part of the movement for propertied unity, has now been elected chairman of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>. Coalfax is backed by the industrial forces on the right of the party, alongside former <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> members. He appears to be focused on fostering closer cooperation with the array of parties between the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> and the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>.

However, Coalfax has thus far proven to be an ineffectual leader, often capitulating to the right wing of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>. Recently, we’ve observed a deterioration in relations with his party, alongside a noticeable rightward shift in the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>'s internal politics.

@deadlock
title: The vote has been deadlocked!
subtitle: No candidate is able to gather a sufficient amount of votes.
view-if: lvp_deadlock

The vote has been deadlocked, with no candidate ahead by enough to constitute a majority. You, the player, now has free will to choose a compromise candidate. Spend it wisely.

- @dietrich_compromise: Albrecht Dietrich.
- @curtius_compromise: Julius Curthose.

@dietrich_compromise
go-to: dietrich

@curtius_compromise
view-if: not curtius_resign_lvp and not (curtius_banking_crisis and banking_crisis_seen)
go-to: curtius

